    description: "Per ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_04072026_1407.md 'Costs to flag honestly' §1 and §3: rust-analyzer is tens of MB of native binary and requires a working Rust toolchain plus resolvable dependencies. It must be **optional**, and the hypergumbo-lang-rust-analyzer backend must degrade gracefully to the tree-sitter rust.py analyzer in three failure modes:\n\n1. rust-analyzer not on PATH (nothing installed)\n2. cargo metadata fails (e.g., private deps unresolvable, weird target triple)\n3. rust-analyzer scip returns non-zero or produces an invalid SCIP file\n\n**Installation path:** add to hypergumbo add-extras (if that is the canonical extras-install surface) with a well-documented opt-in. Alternatively, follow the same PATH-detection pattern grammars already use — pick whichever is already established for large optional native deps.\n\n**Testing:** per the optional-dependency testing playbook — one mock test for the 'unavailable' code path; the real tests run end-to-end when rust-analyzer is installed in CI.\n\n**Observable behavior:** when rust-analyzer is unavailable, the Rust analysis still runs (via rust.py), but the behavior map should carry a provenance marker indicating which backend was used so downstream tools can trust-weight accordingly.\n\nBlocked on the hypergumbo-lang-rust-analyzer package scaffold."  # 475b
    fields: {}  # 475b
